  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive Emergency Response for Older Men and Women affected by Tropical Storm Ana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For an efficient response which will best fit to the beneficiaries&apos; needs in the context of floods, as well as preparing them for the coming rain season, this project will address to the most urgent needs throughout the community outreach team, which will consist of involving the affected communities through community volunteers, an approach that will allow the communities to be owners of the project, and also be able to continue developing it after the its exit. The project will cover 2500 households predominantly older women and men (60+), including older people with disabilities and their care givers of the affected people in Moatize district, thorugh intervention on Food Security and Livelihood; Protection;Disaster Risk Management/Covid-19.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To address suffering caused by Tropical storm Ana in Moatize district, tete province.</narrative>
  </description>
